title: mf_sync
tags: [[Reserved field]] [[Data model]]
kind: reference
summary: Whether metafolder (internal, the default) or another tool (external) owns this content during sync; inherited down mfr_path.

`internal` (the default) or `external`. An external subtree's content is owned by an
outside tool — a git checkout, an `rsync` —: a sync copies its fields but does no
file operation for it, and reports where its files differ between the two sides
([[What sync copies]]). Like `mf_watch` it is inherited down the `mfr_path` tree:
the nearest ancestor that sets it wins, and `GET …/mf-sync` answers the effective
mode ([[Sync endpoints]]). It is synced like any `mf_*` field, so the two sides agree
on it before any file is touched. Setting it needs `force`.
